# DevSecOps + AppSec (adapted)

Source: [awesome-cursorrules security-devsecops](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules).

## Secrets & session

- Never hardcode secrets, credentials, or API keys.
- Never commit `.auth/`, `.env`, cookies, tokens, or credential files.
- Never log session tokens, cookies, or auth paths with secrets.
- Enable `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` (gitleaks on commit when installed).

## Dependencies

- Prefer Node built-ins and already-installed packages; do not add deps without need.
- Before adding a package: `npm view <name> version`. After install/bump: `npm audit`.
- CI fails on `npm audit --audit-level=high` — treat as a gate.

## Input & destructive actions

- Validate CLI args and interactive answers at trust boundaries.
- Delete/download flows need explicit confirmation; do not bypass prompts.
- Prefer Playwright locators over `page.evaluate` with untrusted strings; avoid `eval` / shell `exec` of user input.

## Scope note

Database/RBAC/WAF sections from the upstream rule do not apply — this is a local Playwright CLI, not a server app.
